<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema
  xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
  elementFormDefault="unqualified"
  attributeFormDefault="unqualified"
  version="0.1">

  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation xml:lang="en">
      Draft Strata Football XML structure modeled from the supplied 40749.XML
      NCAA In-Arena Utility fbgame document.

      This is an instance-derived starting contract. It captures every observed
      element family and attribute while leaving context-dependent play and
      player fields optional. Additional provider samples should be compared
      before this draft is treated as a complete interchange specification.

      Live status is carried by the downtogo element. The supplied downtogo is
      complete even though the conditional flag and review attributes are
      absent. Each attribute is emitted with value "Y" only while its condition
      is active; absence means false, and a serialized "N" is invalid.
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>

  <xs:simpleType name="YesNoType">
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="Y"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="N"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="HomeVisitorType">
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="H"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="V"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="PresentYesType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>
        Presence means true. The only serializable value is Y; false is
        represented by omitting the attribute.
      </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="Y"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="PlayContextType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>
        Four-item CSV in this order: possession team, down, yards to go, spot.
        Possession and spot are strictly side-relative V/H values; the spot is
        V or H followed by the yardline, such as H24. This differs from the
        standalone spot attribute, which uses a team abbreviation and yardline.
        play@context is the state before the play; play@newcontext is the state
        after the play. downtogo@context is the current live state.
      </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:pattern value="[^,]+,[^,]+,[^,]+,[^,]+"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="TeamYardlineSpotType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>
        Team abbreviation followed by the yardline, such as WVS24 or FAI35.
        Unlike a context spot, this value does not use the V/H side indicator.
      </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string"/>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="PlayIdentifierType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>
        Three-item CSV in this order: drive number, play number within that
        drive, cumulative play number for the game.
      </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:pattern value="[0-9]+,[0-9]+,[0-9]+"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="LegacyTokensType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>
        Legacy StatCrew token stream retained for backward compatibility. The
        token grammar is difficult to recreate and is not defined by this XSD;
        consumers should treat this value as opaque compatibility data.

        Confirmed legacy token vocabulary, Set 1:
        - CMT:{Text} is non-conformative free text.
        - Q:{QuarterNumber} marks the start of the specified quarter.
        - T:{Clock} records the time on the game clock.
        - KO:{KickerNum},{ToYardline} records a kickoff.
        - RET:{ReturnerNum},{EndYardline} records a return.
        - TACK:{Num}[,{SecondNum}] records one or two tacklers.
        - RUSH:{Num},{EndYardline}[,{Direction}] records a rush; direction is
          optional.
        - PEN:{Team},{PenaltyAbbreviation},{Disposition},{PlayerOrTM},
          {FinalYardline},{DownCode} records a penalty. Disposition is A for
          accepted, D for declined, or O for off-setting. FinalYardline is the
          resulting V/H-relative yardline after enforcement. DownCode is N for
          normal/repeat down in Strata, + for loss of down, or 1 for an
          automatic first down.
        - D:{Down},{ToGo} forces a specific down and distance when ambiguous.
        - {DRIVE}:{Clock} records the drive start time.

        Confirmed legacy token vocabulary, Set 2:
        - PASS:{Passer},{Disposition},{ReceiverOrIntendedReceiver},
          {FinalYardlineOrAsterisk}[,{Direction}] records a passing play.
          Disposition is C for complete, I for incomplete, S for sack, F for
          fumble, or X for intercepted. An incomplete pass uses * instead of a
          final yardline. Direction is optional.
        - PAT records a point-after attempt. Type is K for kick, R for rush, or
          P for pass. Disposition is G for good, M for missed, B for blocked, F
          for fumbled, or X for intercepted. PAT misses do not encode a miss
          direction.
          Kick forms are PAT:K,{Kicker},G, PAT:K,{Kicker},M, and
          PAT:K,{Kicker},B. A blocked kick also emits BLOCK:{Blocker}.
          A successful pass uses PAT:P,{Passer}/{Receiver},G. A failed pass uses
          PAT:P,{Passer},M. A pass intercepted without a return attempt uses
          PAT:P,{Passer},X.
          A failed interception return uses
          PAT:P,{Passer},X,{Returner},N. A successful interception return uses
          PAT:P,{Passer},X,{Returner},Y.
          Rush forms are PAT:R,{Rusher},G, PAT:R,{Rusher},M, and
          PAT:R,{Rusher},F. Return attempts after a fumble use the same optional
          {Returner},{YOrN} suffix as an interception.
        - BRUP:{Number} records a pass breakup.
        - PUNT:{Punter},{EndYardline} records a punt. A blocked punt uses
          PUNT:{Punter},{EndYardline},B, where B is the blocked disposition.
          Every blocked punt also emits BLOCK:{Blocker} to identify the player
          credited with the block.
        - BLOCK:{Number} records the player who blocked a kick or punt.
        - OB: marks an out-of-bounds result and has no value after the colon.
        - NOPLAY: marks a penalty that negates the entire play, corresponding
          to a previous-spot foul in Strata, and has no value after the colon.
        - FGA:{Kicker},{Distance},{Disposition} records a field-goal attempt.
          Disposition is G for good, M for missed, B for blocked, or R for
          returned.
          A miss continues as FGA:{Kicker},{Distance},M,{BallSpotAfterMiss},
          {MissLocation}. StatCrew prompts for BallSpotAfterMiss. MissLocation
          is L for wide left, R for wide right, S for short, C for crossbar, 1
          for left upright, or 2 for right upright.
          A block continues as FGA:{Kicker},{Distance},B,{RecoveredAt},
          {RecoveringTeam},{RecoveringPlayer}. RecoveringPlayer is TM when the
          recovery is credited to the team. A blocked attempt also emits
          BLOCK:{Blocker}.

        Confirmed legacy token vocabulary, Set 3:
        - DN: means the punt was downed and has no value after the colon.
        - FC:{Number} identifies the player who fair caught the kick.
        - FORCE:{Number} identifies the player who forced the fumble.
        - FUMB:{RecoveringTeam},{RecoverySpot},{RecoveringPlayer} records the
          team, spot, and player associated with a fumble recovery.
        - HALF: marks the end of a half and has no value after the colon.
        - QBH:{Team},{Player} records a quarterback hurry.
        - SACK:{Number}[,{SecondNumber}] records one or two players credited
          with a sack. SACK is used in place of TACK on a sack play.
        - SPOT:{TeamInPossession},{BallSpot},{DriveStartYN} explicitly places
          the ball. All five occurrences in 40749.XML follow this structure: N
          accompanies a quarter start and Y accompanies an explicit drive-start
          ball placement.
        - TB: means touchback and has no value after the colon.
        - TOUT:{HOrV} records a timeout taken by the home or visiting team.
        - +:{Player},{FinalYardline} records a lateral.

        One blocked punt in 40749.XML includes BLOCK but omits the required B
        disposition from PUNT. Treat that record as malformed/inconsistent
        GeniusSports/NLS legacy output, not as a valid blocked-punt alternative.
        Strata producers must emit both the PUNT B disposition and BLOCK token.
      </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string"/>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="PlayTypeCodeType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>
        Play category: R rush, P pass, K kickoff, X point-after attempt,
        # game-control information, E penalty, U punt, and F field-goal
        attempt. F is included because every type F record in 40749.XML is a
        field-goal attempt with a legacy FGA token.
      </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="R"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="P"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="K"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="X"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="#"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="E"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="U"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="F"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

